# W44-65 — `dct_suppress_hint` default-on auto-detection

## Context

Follow-on to W44-63 (`6169ba7b`, opt-in API) which shipped the
`LossyConfig::with_dct_suppress_hint(Option<bool>)` setter gated behind
`content_aware_entropy_mul = true`. W44-64 ledger refresh
(`5a5d17b3`) measured 20 OPEN cells residual after the 9-chunk
W44-54..W44-63 session, with 3 codec_wiki cells (e7 d=4/5/6)
identified as the only closeable cluster via default-on of this hint
(the other 17 OPEN are F-D structural residual, ruled out per
`f_d_residual_exhausted_2026-05-18`).

This chunk promotes the W44-63 discriminator to default-on with a
**tighter** mask1x1 median threshold (99.5 vs the opt-in 95.0) to
keep windows95-class pixel-art byte-identical to pre-W44-65 main.

## What shipped

- **Encoder dispatch change** (`vardct/encoder.rs:2249-2305`): the
  `w44_65_suppress_dct64` decision now fires unconditionally when
  `dct_suppress_hint = None`, using the new
  [`W44_65_DCT_SUPPRESS_MEDIAN_THRESHOLD`] (`>= 99.5`). Previous
  W44-63 logic was gated behind `content_aware_entropy_mul = true`
  AND used the looser `> 95` shared threshold.
- **New constant** `W44_65_DCT_SUPPRESS_MEDIAN_THRESHOLD = 99.5`
  (`vardct/encoder.rs:161-191`) with full rationale documenting the
  encoder-pipeline mask1x1 medians measured for each class:
  - Production screenshots: ≈ 100.013 (saturated max).
  - windows95: ≈ 99.060 (near-saturated pixel-art — must be excluded).
  - All 41 CID22 validation photos: ≤ 92.34.
- **API doc updated** (`api.rs` lines 3711-3754, 5073-5117): semantics
  of `with_dct_suppress_hint` reflect default-on. Added explicit
  "Bitstream change" callout — pre-W44-65 main can be recovered with
  `Some(false)`.
- **Encoder field doc updated** (`vardct/encoder.rs:808-833`):
  `pub dct_suppress_hint: Option<bool>` doc string mirrors the API
  change.
- **W44-65 mask1x1 probe** (`examples/w44_65_mask1x1_probe.rs`,
  `examples/w44_65_encoder_mask1x1_probe.rs`): two probes characterise
  the median distribution. The standalone probe used `srgb_to_xyb` and
  diverged from the encoder by ~17 (windows95: 81.49 standalone vs
  99.06 encoder) due to LUT vs powf and scalar vs SIMD float precision
  in the conversion path. The encoder-pipeline probe (`debug-w44-65`
  feature flag, prints from inside `vardct::encoder`) is the
  authoritative measurement.
- **Debug feature** (`debug-w44-65`): emits one line per encode with
  `mask1x1_median`, `dct_suppress_hint`, and image dimensions. Zero
  runtime cost when feature is off. Used for the threshold tuning;
  retained for future investigation.
- **A/B harness** (`examples/w44_65_default_on_ab.rs`): 22-cell sweep
  comparing pinned (`Some(false)`, pre-W44-65 main) vs default
  (`None`, W44-65). Covers codec_wiki target cells + already-FIXED
  screenshot regression probes + windows95 pixel-art invariant +
  5 photo regression probes.
- **Decoder roundtrip test** (`tests/w44_65_decoder_roundtrip.rs`):
  5 `#[ignore]` tests. Three exercise the codec_wiki target cells
  through both djxl and jxl_cli (jxl-rs); two assert
  byte-equality between pinned and default on windows95 + 1418519
  (worst-case photo at mask1x1_median=92.34).

## Reproducer

```
cd ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-65-screenshot-dct-suppress
cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release --features 'parallel' \
    --example w44_65_default_on_ab

# Manual decoder roundtrip (slow):
cargo test -p jxl-encoder --release --test w44_65_decoder_roundtrip \
    --features 'parallel' -- --nocapture --ignored
```

## Measured impact (`benchmarks/w44_65_default_on_ab_2026-05-19.tsv`)

22-cell harness:

| variant            | total bytes | TOTAL Δ      | wins | regs |
|---                 |---          |---           |---   |---   |
| A pre-W44-65 pinned | 947,728     | —            | —    | —    |
| B W44-65 default-on | 941,434     | **-0.66 %** | 8    | 0    |

**Target cells (codec_wiki e7)**:
- d=4: -1.36 % (closes OPEN — bytes 65830 → 64936)
- d=5: -3.25 % (closes OPEN — bytes 59239 → 57314)
- d=6: -1.59 % (closes OPEN — bytes 53936 → 53078)

**Already-FIXED screenshot deepening**:
- imac_g3 e7 d=4: -0.66 % (137 KB → 136 KB)
- imac_g3 e7 d=5: -1.07 % (120 KB → 119 KB)
- imac_g3 e7 d=6: -0.18 %
- terminal e7 d=4: -0.13 %
- terminal e7 d=5: -0.66 %
- terminal e7 d=6: byte-identical (DCT64 not picked anyway at d=6)

**Pixel-art invariance (windows95)**:
- e7 d=1: byte-identical (50096)
- e7 d=2: byte-identical (39615) — was +1.13 % regression under
  `> 95` threshold before the W44-65 tighter `>= 99.5` threshold.
- e7 d=4: byte-identical (29909) — was -0.26 % win under
  the looser threshold; we accept losing this small win to keep
  windows95 fully byte-identical.

**Photo invariance (all 5 probes byte-identical)**:
- 1189261 (median 69.08), 1418519 (median 92.34, worst case),
  1420710 (median 39.55), 1531677 (median 35.63),
  1025469 (median 76.08): all photos at all tested distances
  produce identical bytes between pinned and default paths
  (`mask1x1_median < 99.5` for every CID22 validation photo).

## Acceptance gates (all PASS)

| Gate | Threshold | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| (a) codec_wiki flips        | 3 cells OPEN→FIXED                | **PASS** (3/3, -1.36/-3.25/-1.59 %) |
| (b) Photo regression        | 0 cells with Δ > +0.05 %          | **PASS** (5/5 byte-identical) |
| (c) Pixel-art regression    | windows95 0 cells regressed       | **PASS** (3/3 byte-identical) |
| (d) Already-FIXED deepening | Screenshot Δ ≤ 0                  | **PASS** (5 wins, 1 byte-identical) |
| (e) Hash-lock invariance    | 36 fixtures byte-identical        | **PASS** (no fixture has median ≥ 99.5) |
| (f) Decoder roundtrip       | djxl + jxl_cli accept all variants | **PASS** (15/15 codec_wiki runs ok) |
| (g) Lib tests               | `cargo test --release --lib`       | **PASS** (1258 passed, 29 ignored) |

## Hash-lock regen count

**0 fixtures**. The 36 in-tree `hash_lock_expected.txt` fixtures
exercise small synthetic content (max 48×48 + noise patterns) where
the mask1x1 median is far below 99.5, so the W44-65 gate never fires.

