## Ledger impact (estimated for W44-66)

| | Pre-W44-65 (W44-64) | Post-W44-65 (predicted) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| OPEN | 20 | 17 (3 codec_wiki cells flip) |
| FIXED | 575 | 578 |
| F-D residual | 17 of 20 | 17 of 17 (100 % residual) |

The 17 remaining OPEN are pure F-D structural residual per
`f_d_residual_exhausted_2026-05-18` (cells on 1420710, 1531677,
1189261 at d=5/6, ruled unfixable on global pipeline). All other
W44-arc closeable wedges are now landed.

## What's NOT shipped

- **No zenanalyze dependency** added to production hot path. The W44-64
  recommendation suggested a `palette_log2_size >= 6` companion gate
  (W23-2 classifier shape) to protect windows95-class pixel-art. The
  W44-65 encoder-pipeline mask1x1 probe showed the tighter threshold
  (`>= 99.5` vs `> 95`) is sufficient on its own. windows95 sits at
  median 99.06, cleanly excluded by `>= 99.5`. Adding zenanalyze
  would buy nothing measurable here while increasing the encoder's
  build-graph + cold-start cost.
- **No threshold tuning per distance** — single global threshold works
  across all tested distances. The W44-62 falsification showed the
  DCT64-overpick signal aligns 1:1 with the screenshot class
  regardless of distance.

